---
// How the contamination guard reaches a verdict.
---

<figure class="fig">
            <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--card); padding: 20px; min-width: 0">
              <div style="display: grid; justify-items: center; min-width: 0; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4">
                <div style="border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--paper); padding: 10px 14px; display: grid; gap: 4px; justify-items: center; text-align: center; max-width: 440px"><span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)">before scoring · training_data vs the evalset's datasets and their sources</span><strong style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem">Did the model train on this dataset?</strong></div>
                <span aria-hidden="true" style="height: 14px; border-left: 1px solid var(--ink)"></span>
                <span class="tree" aria-hidden="true" style="width: 50%; height: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-bottom: 0"></span>
                <div style="width: 100%; display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--f-two); gap: 22px 16px">
                  <div style="display: grid; justify-items: center; align-content: start; min-width: 0">
                    <span style="font: 500 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 7px; border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--card)">No</span>
                    <span aria-hidden="true" style="height: 12px; border-left: 1px solid var(--ink)"></span>
                    <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--paper); padding: 9px 12px; text-align: center; max-width: 300px">Do its pretraining data or a source corpus overlap? <span style="color: var(--muted)">(Common Voice in XLS-R, say)</span></div>
                    <span aria-hidden="true" style="height: 12px; border-left: 1px solid var(--ink)"></span>
                    <span aria-hidden="true" style="width: 50%; height: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-bottom: 0"></span>
                    <div style="width: 100%; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px">
                      <div style="display: grid; justify-items: center; align-content: start; min-width: 0"><span style="font: 500 11px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted); padding: 3px 0 5px">no</span><div style="width: 100%; padding: 9px 10px; display: grid; gap: 4px; justify-items: center; text-align: center; background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--good) 12%, var(--card)); border: 1px solid var(--good)"><code style="font: 500 12px/1.3 var(--mono)">clean</code><span style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.35">Scored as normal</span></div></div>
                      <div style="display: grid; justify-items: center; align-content: start; min-width: 0"><span style="font: 500 11px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted); padding: 3px 0 5px">yes</span><div style="width: 100%; padding: 9px 10px; display: grid; gap: 4px; justify-items: center; text-align: center; background: var(--tint); border: 1px solid var(--rule-2)"><code style="font: 500 12px/1.3 var(--mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere">source_overlap</code><span style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.35">Scored, reported with a warning</span></div></div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div style="display: grid; justify-items: center; align-content: start; min-width: 0">
                    <span style="font: 500 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 7px; border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--card)">Yes</span>
                    <span aria-hidden="true" style="height: 12px; border-left: 1px solid var(--ink)"></span>
                    <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--paper); padding: 9px 12px; text-align: center; max-width: 300px">Are the items it trained on listed? <span style="color: var(--muted)">(a train split scored on its test split counts as clean)</span></div>
                    <span aria-hidden="true" style="height: 12px; border-left: 1px solid var(--ink)"></span>
                    <span aria-hidden="true" style="width: 50%; height: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-bottom: 0"></span>
                    <div style="width: 100%; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px">
                      <div style="display: grid; justify-items: center; align-content: start; min-width: 0"><span style="font: 500 11px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted); padding: 3px 0 5px">yes</span><div style="width: 100%; padding: 9px 10px; display: grid; gap: 4px; justify-items: center; text-align: center; background: var(--tint); border: 1px solid var(--rule-2)"><code style="font: 500 12px/1.3 var(--mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere">overlap_excluded</code><span style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.35">Those items left out, the rest scored</span></div></div>
                      <div style="display: grid; justify-items: center; align-content: start; min-width: 0"><span style="font: 500 11px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted); padding: 3px 0 5px">no</span><div style="width: 100%; padding: 9px 10px; display: grid; gap: 4px; justify-items: center; text-align: center; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--ink)"><code style="font: 500 12px/1.3 var(--mono)">contaminated</code><span style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.35">Refused unless --force; never headline</span></div></div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figcaption><strong>How the guard reaches a verdict.</strong> It compares datasets, not generators: a model trained elsewhere on the TTS system behind an evalset's fakes still gets <code>clean</code>.</figcaption>
          </figure>
